expect: fail

# the IR section is the one that states the rule, and it deliberately stops at the colon: array.eco is
# edited often, and a check that fails whenever a line moves says nothing about where the location came
# from. what matters is that the constant names the file the assert was *written* in - never the one being
# emitted, which is this test's own file
#
# the OUT section carries the line as well, because the harness wants one and an exact match is what it
# offers. if a change to array.eco moves the assert, update the number here; the IR check is the claim

--- OUT --->
1
assertion failed: array index out of range
  at array.eco:708
--- IR --->
CHECK: at array.eco:
